From acbf51f8660c7a7b607b9083f71f23f945f36a82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 18:06:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v1.6.1: Channel-Quality Auto Scan + Clear button + passive
 rchqd monitor

Wireless page (Reaper_Wireless.asp) + do_reaper_wifi_cgi:
- Clear button resets the capture results view without a page reload.
- Auto Scan: user-initiated 6 GHz sweep. Pins each PSC-anchored 320 MHz
  candidate through the existing nvram + restart_wireless path (a live
  wl chanspec set does not stick on a running AP), samples chanim_stats,
  ranks by cleanliness, then restores the pre-scan channel; the user clicks
  Pin best to commit the winner. This is the only httpd path that changes a
  channel - deliberately disruptive, warned before it runs.
- New CGI actions scanstart/scanstop/scandata + chq/chqset; status now
  reports scan + chq_on.

rchqd (new daemon): opt-in (nvram rchq_enable, default 0), READ-ONLY passive
channel-quality monitor. Samples chanim_stats on each radio's CURRENT channel
only (no retune, no restart_wireless), publishes /tmp/reaper_chq/live.json and
raises a soft "degraded" advisory whose remedy is the user running Auto Scan.
Wired into services.c (boot / rc dispatcher / teardown), rc.h, defaults.c, and
the router Makefile (obj-y + install target), modeled on rtrafd.

i18n: RWIF_29-49 added (English) across all 25 language dicts, lockstep.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
